# E2177 - OHOS CI workers may lack a host compiler
id:                     E2177
trigger_tool:           conan|clang|make
phase:                  conan-build|package
error_signature:        a build-machine C compiler is required|host compiler unavailable|scdoc-host
severity:               2
category:               ohos|conan|cross-build|packaging
match_keywords:         target compiler only, host generator, pre-generated man pages, build-machine compiler, cross build
title:                  OHOS CI workers need a source-bound fallback for host-only generators
root_cause:              An OHOS Conan worker may expose only the target compiler and sysroot. A recipe that unconditionally builds a host generator with gcc or cc fails before packaging even though target compilation is valid. Reusing the target compiler for the host helper would create a target-architecture binary that cannot run on the worker.
affected_scope:         Cross-built C/C++ packages that generate documentation or other build outputs with a host executable during an OHOS Conan build.
verification_cmd:       conan create <recipe>; inspect build log for target compile and host fallback; verify generated files and package contents
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:            optional-host-generator-with-source-bound-output
rec_description:        Detect a real build-machine compiler separately from target tools. When it is unavailable, consume checked-in outputs generated from the matching upstream inputs and fail closed if those outputs are missing; never substitute a target compiler for a host executable. Regenerate outputs when a host compiler is available.
rec_command:             host_compiler=$(command -v gcc || command -v cc); if [ -n "$host_compiler" ]; then build_host_generator; else copy_verified_prebuilt_outputs; fi
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               host-generator-optional-prebuilt-man-pages
forbid_1_pattern:       target.*compiler.*host.*generator|use.*target.*clang.*host
forbid_1_reason:        The target compiler produces an OHOS binary that cannot execute on the CI worker.
forbid_1_consequence:   Documentation generation fails later or silently packages unusable output.
forbid_2_pattern:       skip.*man.*page|empty.*documentation
forbid_2_reason:        Omitting required generated outputs changes the package contract.
forbid_2_consequence:   The package is incomplete even if the target ELF compiles.
principles:             P006,P010,P014
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []
doc_file:               doc/E2177.md
last_updated:           2026-09-04
source_event:           scdoc/1.11.3 PR #8252 CI #39446 host compiler failure
source_pr:              pending
source_commit:          6946edbe3aa99bf399e33361458c579038a8c7cd
